/athletes/78793"} "Bill Miller"] " (second at the trials) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78600"} "George Jefferson"] " were also highly considered."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Graber cleared 4.15 (13-7¼), passed 4.20 (13-9¼), but could not get over 4.25 (13-11¼) and had to settle for fourth. Miller, Jefferson, and Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/72558"} "Shuhei Nishida"] " all cleared 4.20, Nishida missing once. At 4.25 and 4.30 (14-1¼), Miller had first-attempt clearances, but Nishida would not go away, making both heights on his third tries. Finally, at 4.315 (14-1¾), Miller secured the gold medal with a third-attempt clearance, while Nishida could not get over the bar. Miller failed three times at the world record height of 4.40 (14-5¼). Nishida was a Los Angeles crowd favorite for his sportsmanship in congratulating Miller."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Best Height Cleared"] [:th {} "Attempts at 4.15 m"] [:th {} "Attempts at 4.20 m"] [:th {} "Attempts at 4.25 m"] [:th {} "Attempts at 4.30 m"] [:th {} "Attempts at 4.315 m"] [:th {} "Attempts at 4.35 m"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "447"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78793"} "Bill Miller"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "4.315"] [:td {} "xxo"] [:td {} "o"] [:td {} "o"] [:td {} "o"] [:td {} "xxo"] [:td {} "xxx"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "294"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/72558"} "Shuhei Nishida"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-fl